    "sillyaluminum:aluminummaking-title": "Mod Mechanic: Aluminum Making",
    "sillyaluminum:aluminummaking-text": "<strong>Aluminum Making</strong><br><i>We spent so long asking ourselves if we could, <br>we never stopped to ask ourselves if we should.</i><br><br>As a quick warning, this is a long crafting chain following what may have been one of the processes to get aluminum out of bauxite without the need for electricity.<br><br>Probably. We're not 100% sure but a chemist friend says it might maybe probably have maybe worked once maybe.<br><br><strong>Okay But Why?</strong><br>For the most part, there isn't a good answer as to why. Mostly just bragging rights.<br><br>For actual uses, it does have some. The <a href=\"handbook://item-ingot-aluminum\">ingots</a> fetch a very nice price from traders, giving you quite the profit, and the <a href=\"handbook://item-metalplate-aluminum\">plates</a> can be used to line lanterns. The <a href=\"handbook://item-armor-body-chain-aluminum\">chain</a> and <a href=\"handbook://item-armor-body-plate-aluminum\">plate</a> armors, whilst not having very good protection, only demands half the sacrifices as other chain or plate armors, and the <a href=\"handbook://item-blade-falx-aluminum\">aluminum falx</a> is on par with a <a href=\"handbook://item-blade-falx-steel\">steel falx</a>, though that's because the aluminum is only decorative, not the blade. Finally, aluminum can be alloyed with <a href=\"handbook://item-ingot-copper\">copper</a> to form <a href=\"handbook://item-ingot-aluminumbronze\">aluminum bronze</a>, a alternative of <a href=\"handbook://item-ingot-meteoriciron\">meteoric iron</a> with better stats but much lower durability.<br><br><strong>Prerequisites</strong><br>Many, many resources are needed for making aluminum. Roughly in order, you'll need <a href=\"handbook://block-sillyaluminum:crop-saltwort-7\">saltwort</a>, <a href=\"handbook://item-lime\">lime</a>, <a href=\"handbook://item-stone-bauxite\">bauxite</a>, <a href=\"handbook://item-salt\">salt</a>, <a href=\"handbook://item-ore-sulfur\">sulfur</a>, <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:ore-pyrolusite\">pyrolusite</a>, and <a href=\"handbook://item-charcoal\">charcoal</a>. You'll also need access to <a href=\"handbook://block-barrel\">barrels</a>, <a href=\"handbook://block-bloomerybase-north\">bloomeries</a>, a <a href=\"handbooksearch://quern\">quern</a>, a <a href=\"handbook://block-pulverizerframe-north\">pulverizer</a> with at least tier 2 pounder caps, and way too much time.<br><br><strong>Soda Ash</strong><br><a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-sodaash\">Soda ash</a> is obtained by taking the <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:sprig-saltwort-raw\">sprigs</a> from <a href=\"handbook://block-sillyaluminum:crop-saltwort-7\">saltwort</a> and waiting for them to <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:sprig-saltwort-dry\">dry</a>. Once dried, the sprigs are <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-saltwortash\">burned</a>, the ashes are washed to remove impurities, and then the mixture is dried again, leaving <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-sodaash\">soda ash</a>. From there, it can be fired in a bloomery to obtain <a href=\"handbook://item-metalbit-sodium\">sodium bits</a>, or mixed with <a href=\"handbook://item-slakedlimeportion\">slaked lime</a> to make <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-causticsoda\">caustic soda</a>.<br><br><strong>Sodium</strong><br>Once you have access to <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-sodaash\">soda ash</a>, it can be converted into <a href=\"handbook://item-metalbit-sodium\">sodium</a> quite easily by smelting the <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-sodaash\">soda ash</a> in a <a href=\"handbook://block-bloomerybase-north\">bloomery</a> + <a href=\"handbook://block-bloomerychimney\">chimney</a>. The <a href=\"handbook://item-metalbit-sodium\">sodium bits</a> can later be used along with <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-aluminum\">muriate of alumina</a> to create<a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-saltyaluminum\">aluminum powder mixed with salt</a>. Alternatively, it can be thrown into some water for a small explosion. If you want a not-as-small explosion, it can be cast into an <a href=\"handbook://item-ingot-sodium\">ingot</a> first.<br><br><strong>Alumina</strong><br><a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-alumina\">Alumina</a> is the final result of the Bayer Process. It is obtained by mixing <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-causticsoda\">caustic soda</a> with <a href=\"handbook://item-crushed-bauxite\">crushed bauxite</a> and <a href=\"handbook://item-limewaterportion\">limewater</a> in a cooking pot to get <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:portion-bauxiteslurry\">bauxite slurry</a>. From there, the slurry must be filtered through sand to filter out the <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-sodiumaluminate\">sodium aluminate</a>, leaving <a href=\"handbook://block-sillyaluminum:redmud\">red mud</a> as a byproduct. Then, <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:ore-gibbsite\">gibbsite</a> must be extracted from the <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-sodiumaluminate\">sodium aluminate</a> by mixing it in water, and waiting for the gibbsite to crystallization out. This process can be massively sped up by <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-gibbsite\">crushing gibbsite</a> you already have and adding it to the mixture as seed crystals. Finally, the crushed gibbsite can be smelted inside a bloomery to obtain <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-alumina\">alumina</a>. Later, it can be used to make <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-aluminumchloride\">muriate of alumina</a>.<br><br><strong>Chlorine Gas</strong><br><a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:portion-chlorinegas\">Chlorine Gas</a> (yes it's a gas, no I'm not too lazy to add an entire gas mechanic for 1 fluid, shush!) is used to make <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-aluminum\">muriate of alumina</a>, one of the final steps towards <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-aluminumchloride\">aluminum powder</a>. It is made by mixing <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:ore-pyrolusite\">pyrolusite</a> (found in hematite deposits) with <a href=\"handbook://item-acid-full-hydrochloric\">hydrochloric acid</a> (obtained by mixing <a href=\"handbook://item-acid-full-sulfuric\">sulfuric acid</a> and <a href=\"handbook://item-salt\">salt</a> in a barrel).<br><br><strong>Aluminum Powder</strong><br><a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-aluminum\">Aluminum powder</a> is the final result of this whole process, and has a few more steps to make from alumina and chlorine gas. First, you must mix the alumina with <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:portion-chlorinegas\">chlorine Gas</a> and <a href=\"handbook://item-powder-charcoal\">powdered charcoal</a> in a cooking pot to make <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-aluminumchloride\">muriate of alumina</a>, then mix that and sodium in a cooking pot to make <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-saltyaluminum\">aluminum powder mixed with salt</a>. From here, all that's left to do is to wash the salt out of the powder by throwing it in water, leaving only the <a href=\"handbook://item-sillyaluminum:powder-aluminum\">powdered aluminum</a> to be cast into whatever mold is desired.<br><br><strong>Alternatives</strong><br>Instead of going through all the work for aluminum, you can instead buy <a href=\"handbook://item-arrow-aluminum\">arrows</a>, the <a href=\"handbook://item-blade-falx-aluminum\">falx blade</a>, and the <a href=\"handbook://item-spear-generic-ornatealuminum\">ornate spear</a> from traders (though for a VERY steep price). In fact, this is the only way to obtain the spear. If you still want the pure metal, you could try your hand at finding some <a href=\"handbook://item-nugget-nativealuminum\">native aluminum ore</a>. Good luck, as it is exceptionally hard to find!"
}
